00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.620
Retired Albertan shows Canadian TFSA investors how to use contribution dates to build custom ETF benchmarks and spot true outperformers. This is Modern Investing Techniques, Episode 212. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with no real money. I'm not a licensed financial advisor and this isn't financial advice. Always do your own research before putting real money to work. Friday's close,

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:34.260
a simulated power corporation of Canada hold and two retail screens you can

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:38.460
run without a Bloomberg terminal. Friday's North American session finished

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:48.700
lower, with the NASDAQ composite at 25,955, down 0.2%. That index is up 11.70% year

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:55.400
to date, and up 16.01% since the practice portfolio opened on March 16, 2026.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:01:04.100
The standard and pours 500 closed at 7,624, down 0.5%, and the Toronto Stock Exchange

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:10.400
Composite closed at 35,788, also down 0.5%.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:16.200
About 14 days ago, we simulated TD on a normal course issuer bid that reduced share count

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:22.840
while capital ratios held, and it closed up 2.78%, a reminder that buyback news can still

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:25.440
underpin evaluation case when the tape is messy.

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:30.700
The Federal Reserve's next interest rate decision is imminent, and traders are watching for

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:32.300
any shift in the path of cuts.

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:37.750
Morgan Stanley Chief Investment Officer Mike Wilson called the correction in its final

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:42.210
innings after the average stock has been in a nasty decline since early June.

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:48.010
Microsoft, Alphabet, and Amazon all report within two days and together represent about

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:53.310
15% of the standard in pours 500, so a single surprise can shove the whole index.

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:58.770
Goldman Sachs data showed global hedge funds posting one of their widest drawdowns since the

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:04.570
pandemic last week, which is another way of saying professional breath looked ugly. A retired

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:10.570
Albertan in a Globe and Mail piece weights several exchange traded funds or ETFs by the dates

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:16.690
and dollar amounts of his tax-free savings account, or TFSA deposits instead of measuring himself

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:21.410
against a static Toronto stock exchange, or Standard and Poor's 500 print.

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:27.330
Custom benchmarking is that rebuild. Each contribution is treated as its own bucket that earns

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:31.930
the return of the mix you would have held from the day the cash arrived. Then the buckets are

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:36.550
summed into a personal hurdle rate. Pull the contribution log from your brokerage,

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:40.730
assign each deposit to the allocation you would actually have owned that morning,

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:46.250
and calculate the blended return against your real holdings. Think of each deposit as a separate

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:51.330
garden bed planted on its own date. You do not score every bed against the city's average

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:56.070
rainfall for the year. You score it against the rain that fell after you put that soil in.

00:02:56.630 --> 00:03:00.690
The method works best when money arrives in clumps around market lows or highs,

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:06.030
because that is exactly when a plane index either flatters you or punishes you for timing you

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:11.990
cannot undo. It fails if you cherry pick friendly ETF weights after the fact, or if you pretend

00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:18.203
rebalancing inside the account is free. You added to your TFSA in uneven lumps last year.

00:03:18.703 --> 00:03:22.983
Some of them when markets were already extended. Your holdings beat a static index.

00:03:23.563 --> 00:03:27.603
Do you call that stock picking or do you rebuild the hurdle from the days the cash arrived

00:03:27.603 --> 00:03:33.283
before you take the credit? I'd rebuild it. A single broad index is not a fair picture of the cash

00:03:33.283 --> 00:03:38.323
flows you actually lived. And skipping the rebuild is how people credit or blame a ticker for

00:03:38.323 --> 00:03:41.643
results that were mostly the calendar of new TFSA room.

00:03:42.163 --> 00:03:47.203
A useful habit is to export that log once a quarter, run the weighted math in a simple

00:03:47.203 --> 00:03:51.763
spreadsheet before you review any name, and look for drift between the mix you meant to

00:03:51.763 --> 00:03:53.383
hold and what is sitting there now.

00:03:53.983 --> 00:03:57.623
Remember, cash has a birthday, and the hurdle rate should share it.

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:04.364
Power Corporation of Canada ticker POW on the Toronto Stock Exchange is today's simulated

